  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Can we have an AngularX float for our animator controller parameters by default? The idea would be to have it keep track of how high or low we're looking (1.00 would be the highest and -1.00 would be the lowest) this could be used for a variety of functions within the avatar like having an object near us be able to look up or down without having to keep head tracking enabled, or when flight collisions are made to follow head tracking, instead they could be adjusted with this parameter, it could also be used for some aiming blendtree goodness for when the head tracking is disabled, and for some of us it could even completely remove the need for any form of tracking on our avatars (like for example, if the rig wasn't originally meant to be humanoid, or for non-VR users with animations on their avatar, not to mention for projectile aiming)\n\nThe lack of an angularX parameter has been a bit of a downer for me personally (though my reasons may not be the most popular), especially when we have the Upright, AngularY and other velocity related parameters, and since it seems like the game already keeps track of our view pitch in multiple ways, I figured adding it as a parameter could be a quick harmless addition that'd lead to lots of possibilities in the future.",
